WEBVTT

00:00:32.491 --> 00:00:36.787
For my next trick,
notice I have nothing up my sleeves

00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:39.831
and nothing in my head.

00:00:42.209 --> 00:00:45.254
So, if my lovely assistant
will kindly supply me

00:00:45.337 --> 00:00:48.715
with an ordinary,
non-fake pitcher of milk...

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.263
Behold! The milk has vanished.

00:00:54.346 --> 00:00:57.182
Exiled, perhaps, to another dimension.

00:00:58.809 --> 00:00:59.810
Amazing.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.187
That's why they call you
Bender the Magnificent.

00:01:02.271 --> 00:01:03.272
No, it isn't.

00:01:05.399 --> 00:01:06.400
Whoa.

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:09.695
They discovered an intact
20th-century pizzeria,

00:01:09.778 --> 00:01:11.363
just like the one I used to work at.

00:01:11.446 --> 00:01:12.698
Interesting.

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:13.866
No, wait, the other thing.

00:01:13.949 --> 00:01:14.950
Tedious.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.034
Let's go check it out.

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:17.953
You can see how I lived before I met you.

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:19.788
You lived before you met me?

00:01:19.872 --> 00:01:21.623
Sure, lots of people did.

00:01:21.707 --> 00:01:23.041
Really?

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:38.015
Truly, they were as gods,
who built this place.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.099
Next,

00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:43.270
we come to the splendidly preserved
wooden pizza paddle.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.607
Scientists theorize

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:50.152
it was used to gently
discipline the delivery boy.

00:01:52.905 --> 00:01:54.114
Wait a second.

00:01:54.198 --> 00:01:55.240
This is Panucci's.

00:01:55.324 --> 00:01:57.659
I used to work in this exact pizzeria.

00:01:57.743 --> 00:01:59.494
And for your information, lady,

00:01:59.578 --> 00:02:01.997
this was not just used to paddle my butt.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.208
It was also used to move pizzas
and crush rats.

00:02:04.291 --> 00:02:06.710
I don't know
where you get your facts, sir,

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:11.256
but I am a volunteer housewife
with 45 minutes of orientation

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.301
and a Harlequin romance
about archaeologists.

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:16.553
Don't wave your fancy degrees at me.

00:02:16.637 --> 00:02:18.639
I recognize all this stuff.

00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:20.599
Petrified sausages,

00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:21.892
old Mr. Vitelli,

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.519
and that's...

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:30.108
Yes?

00:02:30.192 --> 00:02:32.653
Pizza delivery for a Mr...

00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:33.779
Seymour Asses.

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:36.198
There's no one by that name here.

00:02:36.281 --> 00:02:37.699
Or anywhere.

00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:40.827
I hope that in time
you'll realize what an idiot you've been.

00:02:40.911 --> 00:02:42.538
I wouldn't count on that.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.088
Aw. Poor little guy.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:53.006
You look like
you haven't eaten in a month.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.341
Here.

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:57.302
But if Mr. Panucci asks,
your name is Seymour Asses.

00:02:59.847 --> 00:03:01.056
I like you, Seymour.

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:04.059
You're not constantly judging me
like all the other dogs.

00:03:04.142 --> 00:03:05.477
Are you?

00:03:06.645 --> 00:03:08.939
Nah. We understand each other.

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:12.276
People think you're just
a dumb mutt who smells bad,

00:03:12.359 --> 00:03:14.945
can't find a girlfriend
and has a crummy job.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:18.031
But you're keeping it real
and you call no man "mister."

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.493
Well, goodbye.

00:03:21.577 --> 00:03:23.161
Live long and prosper.

00:03:32.421 --> 00:03:33.422
Blech.

00:03:33.505 --> 00:03:36.383
That's the least appetizing
calzone I've ever seen.

00:03:36.466 --> 00:03:38.177
No, that's my dog in there.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.761
It's an outrage, I say.

00:03:41.096 --> 00:03:42.347
Hey...

00:03:42.431 --> 00:03:43.682
Ow.

00:03:43.765 --> 00:03:46.977
I'm taking him home and I'd like to see
anyone try and stop me. Uh-oh.

00:03:52.024 --> 00:03:54.276
And then he was ejected by the guards.

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:56.945
Needless to say, I was mortified.

00:03:57.029 --> 00:03:59.448
Well, it's not right to make
my dead pet an exhibit.

00:03:59.531 --> 00:04:00.866
That's like digging up Lassie

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:02.784
and putting her on display in the Louvre.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:04.661
Lassie is on display in the Louvre.

00:04:04.745 --> 00:04:05.787
I know.

00:04:05.871 --> 00:04:08.332
I was deliberately describing
a similar situation.

00:04:08.415 --> 00:04:10.125
Why don't you try protesting?

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:11.960
Like those native Martians.

00:04:12.044 --> 00:04:16.131
Always whining that people don't treat
their ancestors bones with respect.

00:04:17.674 --> 00:04:19.635
Eh, protesting never works.

00:04:19.718 --> 00:04:20.719
You're right.

00:04:20.802 --> 00:04:21.970
I'll give it a shot.

00:04:23.347 --> 00:04:24.806
What do you want?

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.099
Fry's dog!

00:04:26.183 --> 00:04:27.559
When do you want it?

00:04:27.643 --> 00:04:28.769
Fry's dog!

00:04:30.521 --> 00:04:33.315
I will now perform
my people's native dance.

00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:37.444
Do the Hustle...

00:04:42.074 --> 00:04:44.451
It says here that this part of The Hustle

00:04:44.535 --> 00:04:48.080
implores the gods to grant a favor,
usually a Trans Am.

00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:55.671
I'm walking on sunshine, oh-oh

00:04:59.758 --> 00:05:03.428
I'm walking on sunshine, whoa-oh

00:05:03.512 --> 00:05:04.763
That-a-boy, Seymour.

00:05:04.847 --> 00:05:06.723
Right here waiting for me as always.

00:05:06.807 --> 00:05:08.809
Just like that huge mushroom in my shower.

00:05:13.021 --> 00:05:15.065
Hey, there's our little mascot.

00:05:16.275 --> 00:05:18.777
Aw, you've been swimming
in the sewer again?

00:05:18.861 --> 00:05:19.862
You rascal.

00:05:24.199 --> 00:05:25.409
Fry, clean up.

00:05:25.492 --> 00:05:26.827
Seymour, clean up.

00:05:28.662 --> 00:05:29.830
Good dog.

00:05:29.913 --> 00:05:31.498
That's a good Seymour.

00:05:34.084 --> 00:05:36.628
Yo, there's dog fur on my slice.

00:05:36.712 --> 00:05:38.213
Nah, that's vermicelli.

00:05:38.297 --> 00:05:39.631
No fur in here.

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:48.015
He's so cute.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:50.893
He can do two things at one time,
eat and swim.

00:05:50.976 --> 00:05:52.352
Ooh, three things.

00:05:58.317 --> 00:06:00.194
Fry, it's been three days.

00:06:00.277 --> 00:06:02.237
You can't keep boogying like this.

00:06:02.321 --> 00:06:04.281
You'll come down with a fever
of some sort.

00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:06.909
Mr. Fry, I'm Dr. Ben Beeler,

00:06:06.992 --> 00:06:08.952
the paleontologist
who discovered your dog,

00:06:09.036 --> 00:06:11.496
or as some call it, the Beelersaurus.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:12.915
So do I get Seymour back?

00:06:12.998 --> 00:06:14.708
Are you caving to political pressure?

00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:16.043
No. We're sorry,

00:06:16.126 --> 00:06:18.754
but there's just
too much that fossil can teach us

00:06:18.837 --> 00:06:20.506
about dogs from your time.

00:06:20.797 --> 00:06:22.508
His name was Seymour.

00:06:22.591 --> 00:06:25.928
He was once intimate with the leg
of a wandering saxophonist.

00:06:26.011 --> 00:06:28.347
He had wet dog smell,even when dry.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:31.141
And he was not above chasing
the Number 29 bus.

00:06:31.225 --> 00:06:32.935
The 29? Interesting.

00:06:33.018 --> 00:06:34.978
- That's all I needed. Ray?
- I'm good.

00:06:35.062 --> 00:06:37.940
Okay, then, here's your dog back.

00:06:39.316 --> 00:06:40.400
Seymour!

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:45.322
Lady and gentleman,

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:48.867
how about a hand for my
temporary replacement assistant!

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.539
I was all in this part.

00:06:53.622 --> 00:06:54.623
It's magic.

00:06:54.706 --> 00:06:58.877
You're not fit to wear Fry's leotard!

00:06:58.961 --> 00:07:00.337
Stop!

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.880
Good news, everyone.

00:07:01.964 --> 00:07:03.423
Hooray, he's back!

00:07:03.507 --> 00:07:06.218
And he's looking
for a garbage can to put the rock in.

00:07:06.301 --> 00:07:07.386
Here you go, buddy.

00:07:07.469 --> 00:07:11.932
No, actually we've discovered
that Fry's dog was fast-fossilized,

00:07:12.015 --> 00:07:13.809
preserving its cellular structure.

00:07:13.892 --> 00:07:16.103
Which means we can clone it.

00:07:16.186 --> 00:07:17.855
Seymour will live again!

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:20.107
A little land mammal.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.567
Can you believe it, Bender?

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.777
I'm going to havemy best friend back.

00:07:42.421 --> 00:07:44.339
Why the idiot convention?

00:07:44.423 --> 00:07:47.134
Ah, Cubert, my precious babe.

00:07:47.217 --> 00:07:49.887
I'm going to attempt to clone Fry's dog

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:53.432
using the very same apparatus
I used to clone you.

00:07:53.515 --> 00:07:54.933
Ooh, look.

00:07:55.017 --> 00:07:57.519
There's a smidge of toe still in here.

00:07:59.229 --> 00:08:03.192
You see, beneath the fossil's
crunchy mineral shell,

00:08:03.275 --> 00:08:06.570
there's still a creamy core of dog nougat.

00:08:06.653 --> 00:08:09.698
So will Seymour remember
how to sing Walking on Sunshine?

00:08:09.781 --> 00:08:11.450
Amazingly, yes.

00:08:11.533 --> 00:08:16.121
In cases of rapid fossilization,
I can press this brain-scan button,

00:08:16.205 --> 00:08:20.167
retrieving Seymour's memories
at the precise instant of doggy death.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.127
I'm going to get my puppy back.

00:08:22.211 --> 00:08:23.879
In your face, Grim Reaper!

00:08:23.962 --> 00:08:25.964
Crappy, ineffective reaper.

00:08:26.048 --> 00:08:29.635
I just need to reset
the Clone-o-Mat from human mode

00:08:29.718 --> 00:08:30.969
to dog mode.

00:08:32.262 --> 00:08:34.681
The dog says...

00:08:34.765 --> 00:08:37.059
Oh-oh, this may take a while.

00:08:43.857 --> 00:08:46.151
You stink, loser!

00:08:46.235 --> 00:08:48.779
Hey, Fry, pizza going out.

00:08:48.862 --> 00:08:50.239
Come on!

00:08:50.322 --> 00:08:52.282
But I'm celebrating New Year's Eve.

00:08:52.366 --> 00:08:54.451
Like you got squat to celebrate.

00:08:54.535 --> 00:08:56.453
You're a delivery boy this millennium

00:08:56.537 --> 00:08:58.789
and you'll be a delivery boy
next millennium.

00:09:04.086 --> 00:09:05.128
What's with Seymour?

00:09:05.212 --> 00:09:06.547
It's like he don't want you to go

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:08.841
or he thinks your pants
is too short or something,

00:09:08.924 --> 00:09:11.134
which is crazy,
because frankly, you look fabulous.

00:09:11.218 --> 00:09:12.636
Now get going!

00:09:15.681 --> 00:09:17.349
I won't be gone long, Seymour.

00:09:17.432 --> 00:09:19.017
Just wait here till I come back.

00:09:30.904 --> 00:09:33.657
Hello, pizza delivery for...

00:09:36.368 --> 00:09:37.911
Aw, crud.

00:09:40.831 --> 00:09:43.458
Here's to another lousy millennium.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.254
Five, four,

00:09:47.337 --> 00:09:49.548
three, two...

00:09:56.763 --> 00:09:57.764
What the...

00:10:04.146 --> 00:10:05.522
A dog collar for me?

00:10:05.606 --> 00:10:07.024
You shouldn't have.

00:10:07.107 --> 00:10:08.567
That's for Seymour.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:09.818
Oh.

00:10:11.904 --> 00:10:14.781
Say, why'd you get me
a subscription to the Daily Growl?

00:10:14.865 --> 00:10:16.950
That's not a reputable journal of opinion.

00:10:17.034 --> 00:10:18.410
Oh, that's also for Seymour.

00:10:18.493 --> 00:10:20.495
I'm getting everything
ready for when he's cloned.

00:10:20.579 --> 00:10:21.872
Are you on the junk, Fry?

00:10:21.955 --> 00:10:24.917
Why are you wasting time
on a creature of inferior intelligence?

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.044
Hey, he was smart.He could fetch.

00:10:27.127 --> 00:10:28.212
I can fetch.

00:10:32.716 --> 00:10:33.926
He could dig up bones.

00:10:34.009 --> 00:10:35.844
Hello. Charlemagne?

00:10:38.013 --> 00:10:40.516
Plus, I bet he couldn't create
a laser show with his head.

00:10:44.853 --> 00:10:47.231
Look, Bender,
this has nothing to do with you.

00:10:47.314 --> 00:10:48.607
That's impossible!

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:51.610
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I'm working on Seymour's doghouse.

00:10:55.197 --> 00:10:57.783
No one ever asks if Bender
would like to live

00:10:57.866 --> 00:10:59.159
in a tiny little house.

00:10:59.243 --> 00:11:00.619
Not that I would.

00:11:00.702 --> 00:11:03.205
A tiny little house
that says "Bender" on it.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:06.208
Ow!

00:11:09.837 --> 00:11:10.838
This is Fry.

00:11:10.921 --> 00:11:12.881
If you're calling
about the used towels for sale,

00:11:12.965 --> 00:11:15.050
they're still available for $45 each.

00:11:16.593 --> 00:11:18.637
Phil, it's your father. Where are you?

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.556
You're holding up New Year's brunch.

00:11:20.639 --> 00:11:22.432
Your brother can't wait any longer.

00:11:22.516 --> 00:11:25.936
Hello, first bologna
of the new millennium.

00:11:27.521 --> 00:11:29.022
Ah, here he comes.

00:11:29.106 --> 00:11:30.232
That's him and Seymour.

00:11:32.609 --> 00:11:33.861
Well, that's weird.

00:11:33.944 --> 00:11:35.195
Seymour's here, but...

00:11:35.279 --> 00:11:37.906
Go! Go! Touchdown!

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:38.991
But where's Philip?

00:11:39.074 --> 00:11:42.035
I'm telling you,
the Y2K computer's got him.

00:11:42.119 --> 00:11:45.622
We'll face burning roads,
rivers exploding,

00:11:45.706 --> 00:11:48.792
calculators transformed
into Scud missiles.

00:11:48.876 --> 00:11:50.627
There's nothing we can do.

00:11:55.674 --> 00:11:57.050
What's that, Seymour?

00:11:57.134 --> 00:11:58.552
You walking on sunshine?

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:04.349
He's trying to tell us something.
Maybe he can lead us to Philip.

00:12:05.851 --> 00:12:07.227
Should we follow him?

00:12:07.311 --> 00:12:09.438
To our deaths? Negatory.

00:12:10.063 --> 00:12:14.067
It's the Y2K trying to lure us
into an ambush, and I ain't buying it.

00:12:14.151 --> 00:12:15.402
Pass the bologna.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:28.123
Are you two going to be done soon?

00:12:28.207 --> 00:12:30.959
Sorry, but we need to practice
hand-to-hand combat

00:12:31.043 --> 00:12:33.086
in case an enemy knocks the laser guns

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:36.006
out of our hands
and they slide way across the room.

00:12:36.089 --> 00:12:37.674
Well, could you do it someplace else?

00:12:37.758 --> 00:12:39.384
I'm setting up Seymour'sdoggie bed.

00:12:39.468 --> 00:12:41.929
- Okay.
- Ow!

00:12:47.476 --> 00:12:48.727
Heel, boy, heel.

00:12:49.228 --> 00:12:50.729
Oh, hello, Fry.

00:12:50.812 --> 00:12:52.356
I guess I didn't notice you there.

00:12:52.439 --> 00:12:54.942
I'm having such fun
with my new best friend,

00:12:55.025 --> 00:12:56.193
Robo-Puppy.

00:12:56.276 --> 00:12:57.486
That's nice.

00:12:57.569 --> 00:12:58.987
I was just out walking him.

00:12:59.071 --> 00:13:00.614
Yes, you can walk him.

00:13:00.697 --> 00:13:03.992
Of course, after he goes,
you have to refill the canisters.

00:13:04.076 --> 00:13:06.620
Come here, boy. Pet, pet, pet.

00:13:06.703 --> 00:13:08.372
Robo-Puppy receiving petting.

00:13:08.455 --> 00:13:11.375
Bender, are you jealous of Fry's puppy?

00:13:11.458 --> 00:13:13.210
That's so adorable.

00:13:13.293 --> 00:13:17.548
Jealous? Not when I have
the love of Robo-Puppy here.

00:13:17.631 --> 00:13:19.758
Robo-Puppy, lick my cheek.

00:13:19.842 --> 00:13:23.262
Robo-Puppy preparing to lick cheek.

00:13:23.345 --> 00:13:26.223
Robo-Puppy commencing cheek licking.

00:13:26.306 --> 00:13:27.558
Licking in progress.

00:13:27.641 --> 00:13:29.017
Licking complete.

00:13:29.142 --> 00:13:32.646
Robo-Puppy truly is
robot's best friend, huh?

00:13:32.729 --> 00:13:34.439
Ah! There, perfect.

00:13:37.442 --> 00:13:39.152
Good news, everyone.

00:13:39.236 --> 00:13:41.154
The Clone-o-Mat is ready!

00:13:43.824 --> 00:13:44.867
Finally.

00:13:46.201 --> 00:13:49.413
Robo-Puppy commencing
two hour yipping session.

00:13:55.043 --> 00:13:56.962
Robo-Puppy mistreatment alert!

00:13:57.045 --> 00:13:58.964
Robo-Puppy mistreatment alert!

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:05.304
Behold once more, the mighty Clone-o-Mat.

00:14:05.387 --> 00:14:08.974
Requiring such vast amounts
of electricity that we must

00:14:09.057 --> 00:14:12.519
harness the elemental power
of nature itself.

00:14:15.105 --> 00:14:16.773
I speak, of course,

00:14:16.857 --> 00:14:20.277
of molten lava deep within
the Earth's core.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.196
To the subbasement.

00:14:37.336 --> 00:14:39.046
Powering up Clone-o-Mat.

00:14:41.215 --> 00:14:44.009
Placing fossil on the plat-clone-o-form.

00:14:47.054 --> 00:14:49.681
Initiating dog brain CAT scan.

00:14:52.684 --> 00:14:54.520
Come on, boy, come back to life.

00:14:54.603 --> 00:14:59.316
Know ye now what it feels like
to be Dog God.

00:14:59.942 --> 00:15:03.278
Commencing DNA extraction.

00:15:09.576 --> 00:15:11.787
Fry, come on, the talent show.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:13.539
What? I'm in the middle of something.

00:15:13.622 --> 00:15:17.543
But if we don't perform,
in what sense do we have an act?

00:15:17.626 --> 00:15:19.670
Bender, enough. Leave me alone.

00:15:20.546 --> 00:15:22.422
So that's how it is, huh?

00:15:22.506 --> 00:15:24.091
I thought you were my friend,

00:15:24.174 --> 00:15:28.303
but if you love your dog so much
maybe you'd rather play fetch.

00:15:31.223 --> 00:15:32.558
No!

00:15:38.063 --> 00:15:40.566
Now I'm all you got.

00:15:45.195 --> 00:15:47.239
I hate you!

00:15:47.322 --> 00:15:49.867
I hate you, you evil metal man!

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.201
Ow!

00:15:51.827 --> 00:15:53.370
So anyway, your dog is melted.

00:15:53.453 --> 00:15:54.746
Now we're friends again.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:56.206
Not necessarily,

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.041
for the dog may yet survive.

00:15:58.125 --> 00:15:59.626
May yet? Really?

00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:00.794
Indeed.

00:16:00.878 --> 00:16:03.297
You see, that fossilwas made of dolomite,

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:06.049
the tough black mineralthat won't cop out

00:16:06.133 --> 00:16:07.801
when there's heat all about.

00:16:07.885 --> 00:16:12.389
By contrast, observe the lava's effect
on this ice swan.

00:16:15.434 --> 00:16:18.604
Of course, that would have melted
even at room temperature.

00:16:18.687 --> 00:16:20.230
I just wanted to get rid of it.

00:16:20.314 --> 00:16:23.609
But had it been made of that
righteous mineral dolomite,

00:16:23.692 --> 00:16:26.320
there's a slim chance
it might have survived.

00:16:26.403 --> 00:16:28.363
So Seymour might still exist?

00:16:28.447 --> 00:16:30.324
Perhaps, for a few minutes.

00:16:30.407 --> 00:16:31.992
It's dolomite, baby.

00:16:32.075 --> 00:16:34.161
Then I'm going in after him.

00:16:38.415 --> 00:16:40.292
He'd come after me.

00:17:25.003 --> 00:17:27.548
Acting like a moron
won't bring your dog back.

00:17:27.631 --> 00:17:29.174
Then all hope is lost.

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.595
Goodbye, Seymour.

00:17:36.974 --> 00:17:38.684
Please stop crying, Fry.

00:17:39.059 --> 00:17:40.227
Here.

00:17:41.353 --> 00:17:44.439
I assumed you were just pretending
to love the dog

00:17:44.523 --> 00:17:46.316
to toy with my emotions.

00:17:46.817 --> 00:17:48.777
Oh, what have I done?

00:17:48.861 --> 00:17:50.153
You didn't do anything.

00:17:50.237 --> 00:17:51.655
Don't beat yourself up.

00:17:51.738 --> 00:17:53.615
Fry, I'm sorry.

00:17:53.699 --> 00:17:55.951
I should have understood
how someone can love

00:17:56.034 --> 00:17:59.037
an inferior creature, because I love you.

00:17:59.121 --> 00:18:00.873
Not in the way of the ancient Greeks,

00:18:00.956 --> 00:18:03.166
but the way a robot loves a human,

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.960
a human loves a dog,

00:18:05.043 --> 00:18:07.629
and, occasionally,
a gorilla loves a kitty.

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:09.590
I'm going in.

00:18:09.673 --> 00:18:10.924
I'm a professor.

00:18:11.008 --> 00:18:13.051
Why isn't anyone listening to me?

00:18:13.135 --> 00:18:15.262
You can't go in because you'll melt.

00:18:15.512 --> 00:18:18.599
The fossil only has a chance
because it's made of dolomite.

00:18:18.682 --> 00:18:21.226
I'm 40% dolomite.

00:18:25.147 --> 00:18:26.940
Oh, it's hot. Oh, it's very hot.

00:18:37.951 --> 00:18:40.996
Oh, I am one hungover cryogenicist.

00:18:41.079 --> 00:18:43.707
Just throw that mutt in the freezer
till his owners get here.

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:46.335
You can't solve all your problems
by freezing them, boss.

00:18:46.418 --> 00:18:48.504
I think you're forgetting our motto.

00:18:52.341 --> 00:18:55.469
Are you the cryogenicist
who called about our son's dog?

00:18:55.552 --> 00:18:57.262
Oh! You must be the Frys.

00:18:57.346 --> 00:18:58.889
Yeah, he's right over there.

00:18:59.806 --> 00:19:01.141
Sorry we're late.

00:19:01.225 --> 00:19:03.268
We all got sickfrom eating bad bologna.

00:19:03.352 --> 00:19:04.436
Y2K.

00:19:06.647 --> 00:19:08.232
What's he so worked up about?

00:19:08.315 --> 00:19:11.026
He's just upset'cause our boy's missing.

00:19:11.109 --> 00:19:13.654
Come on, you overgrown rat,
lead us to Philip.

00:19:20.702 --> 00:19:22.538
Bender's been down there too long.

00:19:22.621 --> 00:19:23.997
I'm going in after him.

00:19:24.081 --> 00:19:26.667
Professor! Lava! Hot!

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:28.252
This is all my fault.

00:19:28.335 --> 00:19:32.214
I let my best friend risk his life
just to get my dead dog back.

00:19:39.847 --> 00:19:40.848
Bender!

00:19:40.931 --> 00:19:44.726
And that is why they call me
Bender the Magnificent.

00:19:46.395 --> 00:19:47.729
Hey, where'd everybody go?

00:19:50.983 --> 00:19:53.861
- Okay, let's clone us some dog.
- Yeah!

00:19:53.944 --> 00:19:55.112
Very well...

00:19:55.195 --> 00:19:58.365
Let this abomination unto the Lord begin!

00:20:04.162 --> 00:20:05.414
Interesting.

00:20:05.497 --> 00:20:09.251
It seems Seymour died
at the ripe old age of 15.

00:20:09.334 --> 00:20:10.460
Fifteen?

00:20:10.544 --> 00:20:13.714
You mean, he lived for 12 more years
after I got frozen?

00:20:13.797 --> 00:20:14.965
Indeed.

00:20:15.424 --> 00:20:17.050
Stop the cloning.

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:23.140
Oh, sure,smash the smart guy's machine.

00:20:23.223 --> 00:20:24.474
Fry, what's wrong?

00:20:24.558 --> 00:20:25.684
Think about it.

00:20:25.767 --> 00:20:28.145
Seymour lived a full life
after I was gone.

00:20:28.228 --> 00:20:30.647
He probably even added
new songs to his repertoire.

00:20:30.731 --> 00:20:32.065
But that's a good thing.

00:20:32.149 --> 00:20:34.359
Walking on Sunshine sucks noodles.

00:20:34.443 --> 00:20:36.570
I had Seymour till he was three.

00:20:36.653 --> 00:20:39.364
That's when I knew him,
and that's when I loved him.

00:20:40.908 --> 00:20:42.534
I'll never forget him.

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:46.163
But he forgot me a long, long time ago.

00:20:54.671 --> 00:21:01.220
If it takes forever

00:21:01.303 --> 00:21:07.434
I will wait for you

00:21:07.518 --> 00:21:11.897
For a thousand summers

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:16.443
I will wait for you

00:21:16.527 --> 00:21:21.406
Till you're back beside me

00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:25.953
Till I'm holding you

00:21:26.036 --> 00:21:29.665
Till I hear you sigh

00:21:29.748 --> 00:21:32.084
Here in my arms...

00:21:32.167 --> 00:21:33.502
Ow!

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:40.133
If it takes forever

00:21:40.217 --> 00:21:45.639
I will wait for you

00:21:45.806 --> 00:21:49.893
For a thousand summers

00:21:49.977 --> 00:21:54.356
I will wait for you...